    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change I implemented.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe identity key was redesigned from a plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` string into a hashed, soundex-based key, and duplicate detection is now driven solely by that key.\n\n**New identity key** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.identityKey`):\n```\nidentityKey = SHA-256 hex over ( normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName) )\n```\nThe full 64-character lower-case hex digest is used (via a newly-exposed `Sha256Hasher.hex(...)`), so the `identityKey` DTO field now matches `[0-9a-f]{64}`.\n\n**New `Soundex` component** (`rest/validation/Soundex.java`): a standard American Soundex encoder (retain first letter, map consonants to digits, collapse adjacent same-coded letters, `h`/`w` transparent, pad/truncate to 4). Wired into the controller via constructor injection.\n\n**Duplicate detection (409)** \u2014 `rejectDuplicateIdentity` still compares this single key, still ignores owners flagged `deleted` (via `findExistingOwner`), and the email-domain blocklist still runs earlier in `createOwner`, so it's applied first. Because the telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same last name + postcode but **different telephones no longer collide** \u2192 no 409.\n\n**Removed the separate household-duplicate 409 block** \u2014 `rejectHouseholdDuplicate` and its call in `createOwner` are gone. `householdId` itself is retained (still used for household size / membership-level derivation).\n\n**Soft match** (`possibleDuplicateOf`) \u2014 now triggers when the `identityKey` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** `postcode` match. This is exactly the case for two owners with the same household but different telephones: they're created (not rejected) and the second is flagged `possibleDuplicate`.\n\nI also updated the `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` and OpenAPI `identityKey` documentation to describe the new derivation.\n\n## Tests\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 both acceptance checks (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` asserting the 64-hex shape, and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` asserting the 409 on an identical owner) pass. That is the complete test suite in this repo.",
